RTSP registers the mic stream once, when it starts, from the live audio
input: codec, sample rate and AAC config all come from it. Audio changes only
restart the audio thread, so the SDP goes stale:

- prudynt started with the mic disabled has no audio track, and enabling the
  mic later never adds one, not even for new sessions;
- changing mic_format, mic_hq or force_stereo keeps advertising the old
  stream, so every client decodes the new one with the wrong codec (an AAC
  track carrying G.711 after switching formats) until prudynt restarts.

Restart RTSP along with the audio thread when the format, rate or channel
count changes; main brings the audio input up before RTSP, so the track is
registered from the new input. Enabling the mic restarts RTSP only when no
audio track is registered, tracked by global_rtsp_audio_registered, so a
mic toggle (the microphone command, the privacy plugin) keeps connected
sessions as before.

